t's either the best thing ever or  the worst thing ever and so trying to  boil down that kind of nuance into  nothing more than a number  first of all honestly it would just  stress me out I don't like having to  think in terms of of that especially  because once you start using numbered  ratings or any rating system actually  there are people out there and that will  start to basically keep track and then  throw it back in your face  so if for whatever reason I chose to  like we're good again this is regardless  of the context of what I said in the  review if I chose to even Avengers  infinity war and nine and the Godfather  and eight for whatever my reasons might  be for doing that if I did that and  that's not me saying what I would number  those as this is a for instance if I did  that there would be people going oh my  god you think marvel's is better than  The Godfather I'm like oh for God's sake  cuz that's the thing the minute you  assign a number to things people take it  as a as like a hot piece of hard data  but I'm giving opinion an opinion is not  made up of hard data so I don't like  giving anyone the ammunition to try and  break down my thoughts on you know  through the use of quote-unquote hard  data or we know that he liked this  better than and that's another thing  with ratings so like if I'm rating what  do I do with something that I can  recognize was very well done but what it  was doing was not something I enjoy do I  give it more points than my enjoyment  would indicate on its technical  instructional merits do I take something  that I know is a deeply flawed film but  that I loved personally do i dock it  down more do i boost it up up and over  things like I don't I hate the idea of  having to make those calculations and  like the closest I come to doing any of  that is rankings I will do you know  rankings but that's always relic  that's always lumping a bunch of a  similar thing together like ranking the  Marvel movies ranking Doctor Who  